ABOUT THIS LICENCE

This licence allows charities, non-profits, community groups, educational
institutions, academic researchers, students, individuals, and volunteers to
use, modify, and deploy this software freely. It restricts companies from
selling the software or offering it as a commercial hosted service without
permission.


1. GRANT OF RIGHTS

You are granted a free, worldwide, non-exclusive licence to use, copy, modify,
and distribute this software and its source code, provided your use falls
within the categories described in this section.

The following uses are permitted without charge or further agreement:

  (a) Use by registered charities, non-profit organisations, community groups,
      educational institutions, academic researchers, students, teaching staff,
      individuals, and volunteers.

  (b) Deployment on any infrastructure, including cloud providers (such as
      AWS, Azure, or GCP), virtual private servers, Kubernetes clusters,
      on-premises hardware, or personal computers.

  (c) Operation of the software as a public-facing service by a qualifying
      organisation — for example, a charity running the software on the
      internet so that its members, donors, supporters, or the general public
      can access it.


2. PERMITTED ACTIVITIES BY QUALIFYING ORGANISATIONS

To avoid doubt, qualifying organisations (charities, non-profits, community
groups, and educational institutions) may use this software to:

  (a) Collect donations and payments.
  (b) Sell merchandise, event tickets, or memberships.
  (c) Manage fundraising campaigns and charitable programmes.
  (d) Charge membership fees or event registration fees.
  (e) Host the software on the public internet and allow anyone to access it.
  (f) Engage paid staff, contractors, IT consultants, or volunteers to install,
      configure, develop, maintain, or administer the software on their behalf.
  (g) Use the software for academic research, coursework, teaching, or
      university-affiliated projects.

These activities are considered internal use by the qualifying organisation,
even when the public interacts with the service or money changes hands in
the course of legitimate charitable activity.


3. CONTRACTED HOSTING ON BEHALF OF A QUALIFYING ORGANISATION

A third-party provider (such as a hosting company, IT consultancy, managed
service provider, or freelancer) may install, configure, host, operate, and
maintain this software on behalf of a specific qualifying organisation without
requiring a separate commercial licence, provided that:

  (a) The instance is exclusively for that single qualifying organisation's
      own use.

  (b) The qualifying organisation has directly engaged the provider for
      this purpose.

  (c) The provider does not offer this software as a general product or
      service to multiple unrelated customers.

This clause exists so that charities are never forced to host or administer
the software themselves. A charity may pay someone to run it for them.


4. COMMERCIAL USE RESTRICTION

The following activities require a separate written commercial licence from
the copyright holder:

  (a) Offering this software, or a substantially modified version of it, as
      a hosted service to third parties as a general commercial product.

  (b) Selling, sublicensing, or white-labelling this software.

  (c) Bundling this software into a commercial product for resale.

  (d) Operating a managed multi-tenant service that markets this software
      (or a derivative) to multiple customers.

If you are unsure whether your intended use requires a commercial licence,
please contact the copyright holder. We are happy to discuss it.


5. MODIFICATIONS AND REDISTRIBUTION

  (a) You may modify this software for your own use or for use by a
      qualifying organisation.

  (b) You may redistribute this software (modified or unmodified), provided
      that you include a copy of this licence and retain all copyright notices.

  (c) You may not remove or alter the terms of this licence in any
      redistributed copy.

  (d) Contributing modifications back to the project is encouraged but
      not required.


